[00:01.20] Lord Worth Come in!
[00:04.64] Mary Yes, sir?
[00:06.29] Lord Worth No, no Mary... I don't want you!
[00:08.63] Mary Who do you want, sir?
[00:09.60] Lord Worth I want James... I want him immediately!
[00:12.55] Mary Yes, sir... I'll go and find him.
[00:15.38] Lord Worth Ah, James!
[00:16.50] James Did you want to see me, sir?
[00:17.66] Lord Worth Yes, I wanted to see you twenty minutes ago.
[00:21.07] James Sorry, sir. I was in the garage.
[00:23.04] Lord Worth I want a car this afternoon.
[00:24.42] James Which car do you want, sir? The Rolls, the Mercedes, or the Ferrari?
[00:26.94] Lord Worth Mmm... the Rolls, I think. Yes, the Rolls.
[00:28.82] James Where do you want to go, sir?
[00:29.76] Lord Worth Heathrow Airport Terminal 2.
[00:33.09] James What time, sir?
[00:34.88] Lord Worth We'll leave here after lunch... at two o'clock.
[00:37.45] Lord Worth Ah, Charles!
[00:40.22] Charles Yes, sir.
[00:41.23] Lord Worth I want an early lunch today, Charles.
[00:43.94] Charles Yes, sir... What time?
[00:45.11] Lord Worth Twelve o'clock... Oh, and I want you to reserve a table at the Savoy... for seven o'clock.
[00:46.36] Charles Yes, sir.
[00:51.84] Lord Worth And I want Mary to prepare the guest room for Sir Thomas.
[00:56.73] Lord Worth I want her to make a special effort. Sir Thomas is a very important guest.
[01:01.30] Charles Yes, sir... anything else, sir?
[01:05.80] Lord Worth No, Charles, that's all.